---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---
<Legal title="Privacy policy" description="How WhiskerWorks handles your data on this website, in our games and in our live series." updated="October 30, 2026">
  <p>We make games, not data businesses. This policy explains what little we collect, why, and how to have it deleted. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  <h2>This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No cookies and no advertising trackers.</li>
    <li>If enabled, we use privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics (Plausible) that count page views without identifying you.</li>
    <li>Our hosting provider keeps standard server logs (such as IP address and browser) for security, for a short period.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Our games</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No ads and no ad SDKs, so no advertising identifiers.</li>
    <li>Purchases are handled by Apple and Google. We receive a receipt to unlock content, never your payment details.</li>
    <li>Optional features such as cloud sync or leaderboards store a random player ID and the data needed for that feature. Each game’s store listing details exactly what it collects.</li>
    <li>Anonymous crash reports may be collected to fix bugs.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Live series (Flag Wars and others)</h2>
  <p>When you comment on one of our episodes, your public handle and comment are already public on that platform. To run the game we record your public handle, the country you named and the date, and we may show your handle on the live map and in episodes (for example as a country’s Founder). We never ask for or store anything else.</p>
  <p>Want your handle removed? Email us and it will be replaced with “anonymous” at the next daily update.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live (including under the GDPR and CCPA) you can ask to access, correct or delete your data, or object to its use. Email us and we will respond within 30 days. You can also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Our games are made for a general audience and do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13 (or the minimum age in your country).</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy we will update the date at the top of this page.</p>
</Legal>
